1
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,215
<i>But this isn't an isolated incident.</i>

2
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,301
Especially now
that there's someone lurking around,

3
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:53,762
that vigilante you call a manananggal.

4
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:55,096
As much as possible,

5
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:57,557
don't tell anyone about this. Not a soul.

6
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:58,892
<i>Especially Chiara and Mikoy.</i>

7
00:00:58,975 --> 00:01:00,143
They already have enough on their plate.

8
00:01:00,226 --> 00:01:01,895
We don't need to add to it.

9
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:07,358
Now that you've finally said
how you really feel,

10
00:01:07,442 --> 00:01:08,568
not because you'll end up together,

11
00:01:08,651 --> 00:01:09,861
you've won because

12
00:01:09,944 --> 00:01:12,655
you're no longer lying
about how you really feel.

13
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:15,784
So now, enjoy your life.

14
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:22,373
Did you hear about what happened
to ma'am's husband?

15
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:23,374
<i>Viktor Valtrovi?</i>

16
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:25,126
<i>Yes. Apparently, he got badly beaten up.</i>

17
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:27,921
I think we made
the wrong call letting him stay here.

18
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:29,339
HQ is going to come after us for this.

19
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:31,132
General Norberto might find out.

20
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:32,467
Let's go.

21
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:35,345
<i>I have an idea, kids.</i>

22
00:01:35,428 --> 00:01:38,598
Your Godmother Mylene won't be able
to make it to your wedding

23
00:01:42,227 --> 00:01:42,936
Because

24
00:01:43,019 --> 00:01:47,106
Vicky has agreed to be
your wedding godmother.

25
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:48,983
- Really?
- Yes!

26
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:50,735
Thank you so much!

27
00:01:51,861 --> 00:01:52,654
<i>Mama Vicky.</i>

28
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:53,780
There's an update.

29
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:58,493
Viktor and Donabel won't
be able to attend the wedding.

30
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:33,319
Not bad.

31
00:02:35,864 --> 00:02:36,698
Thank you.

32
00:02:43,454 --> 00:02:44,372
Carlota?

33
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:50,420
What are you doing here?

34
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:54,048
Did Senator Quintin send you?

35
00:02:54,632 --> 00:02:56,259
If he sent me,

36
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:58,928
I wouldn't be handing you a tissue.

37
00:03:00,346 --> 00:03:01,180
Donabel.

38
00:03:07,145 --> 00:03:08,146
Let's go.

39
00:03:26,789 --> 00:03:27,665
<i>Where are you?</i>

40
00:03:28,416 --> 00:03:29,626
I'm almost there.

41
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:31,878
<i>Are you sure we're safe?</i>

42
00:03:32,378 --> 00:03:33,421
<i>You weren't followed?</i>

43
00:03:33,963 --> 00:03:36,132
<i>That relationship of yours</i>
<i>could complicate things.</i>

44
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:37,800
<i>She's Viktor's former ally.</i>

45
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:39,636
<i>And now she's an agent.</i>

46
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,595
<i>That's risky.</i>

47
00:03:45,975 --> 00:03:47,060
I'm on my way.

48
00:03:57,237 --> 00:03:59,197
Viktor! Viktor!

49
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:15,588
we still have a long way to go.

50
00:04:17,048 --> 00:04:18,383
Buckle up first.

51
00:04:19,092 --> 00:04:21,261
Wait, where are we going?

52
00:04:21,844 --> 00:04:22,845
Albay.

53
00:04:26,099 --> 00:04:27,016
Wow!

54
00:04:27,976 --> 00:04:29,018
Viktor!

55
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:41,489
I don't know.

56
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:43,199
Maybe

57
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,410
I'm getting old too.

58
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:47,412
Or

59
00:04:48,204 --> 00:04:50,915
maybe I'm getting tired
of counting my enemies.

60
00:04:54,168 --> 00:04:56,212
Besides, I'm not the only one.

61
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:05,054
Cocoy.

62
00:05:05,638 --> 00:05:08,182
So, we're not okay yet, all right?

63
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:11,269
But whenever I get the chance to help,

64
00:05:11,352 --> 00:05:13,146
I'd rather choose to do it.

65
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:18,443
I won't forget this.

66
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:23,239
Because gas is expensive.

67
00:05:35,835 --> 00:05:38,212
Wait. Are you two a thing?

68
00:05:38,296 --> 00:05:39,338
Huh?

69
00:05:40,256 --> 00:05:41,340
No!

70
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:43,092
Ouch.

71
00:05:47,096 --> 00:05:48,097
I'm already dating someone.

72
00:05:48,181 --> 00:05:49,223
Really?

73
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:52,018
Sianong!

74
00:06:53,663 --> 00:06:54,872
Looking good!

75
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:57,041
Looks like you're really all set!

76
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:58,709
Of course.

77
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:01,504
I'm not that skinny, crybaby kid
you once knew anymore.

78
00:07:03,756 --> 00:07:04,882
Oh, and also,

79
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:08,010
before I head to Manila,

80
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:09,428
can I meet Mama V?

81
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:10,721
Come on.

82
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:11,639
It's not allowed.

83
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:17,645
What a shame!

84
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:20,565
You know, it's been so long

85
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:23,568
since the last time we saw each other.

86
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:25,445
Are you even listening?

87
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:26,737
I said you can't.

88
00:07:27,321 --> 00:07:28,531
Besides, it'll be difficult.

89
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:29,657
Everything's already planned out.

90
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:31,868
Even a small change
could affect everything.

91
00:07:32,452 --> 00:07:35,204
I'm just really excited to see her.

92
00:07:44,213 --> 00:07:46,090
The moment we've been waiting for is near.

93
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:47,884
The fulfillment of everything,

94
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:50,386
everything that was destined for us.

95
00:07:50,470 --> 00:07:51,512
Do you know that?

96
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:54,515
We were denied justice.

97
00:07:57,810 --> 00:07:58,811
Why aren't you excited?

98
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:01,189
Are you having second thoughts?

99
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,278
What kind of question is that?

100
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:11,073
You're avoiding the question.

101
00:08:14,452 --> 00:08:15,453
You are.

102
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,663
Be honest with me.

103
00:08:18,247 --> 00:08:19,415
You're having second thoughts, aren't you?

104
00:08:20,124 --> 00:08:23,711
You want to walk away from
everything we've been planning?

105
00:08:25,421 --> 00:08:26,297
Answer me!

106
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,007
What are you talking about?

107
00:08:28,508 --> 00:08:29,634
You're mistaken.

108
00:08:30,927 --> 00:08:32,094
I hope so.

109
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,305
I hope I'm wrong.

110
00:08:34,889 --> 00:08:37,767
Because I know those eyes all too well.

111
00:08:38,434 --> 00:08:40,478
Filled with doubt.

112
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:43,189
I know those movements all too well.

113
00:08:44,607 --> 00:08:48,277
So hesitant, filled with doubt.

114
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:50,655
I know them all too well
because I used to be the same!

115
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:55,117
I used to be like that too, weak.

116
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:58,412
Letting my emotions take over.

117
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:05,503
Here, ma'am, sir. Have a seat.

118
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:09,507
Hey, it's the Eiffel Tower!

119
00:09:11,133 --> 00:09:11,968
Beautiful!

120
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:13,928
The view is beautiful, honey.

121
00:09:27,483 --> 00:09:28,651
The view is amazing, isn't it?

122
00:09:31,779 --> 00:09:32,989
But of course,

123
00:09:33,072 --> 00:09:35,866
in my eyes, you're the most beautiful!

124
00:09:36,951 --> 00:09:38,494
You're something else, Sean.

125
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:41,205
I'm really your number one fan!

126
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:42,331
Of course.

127
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:46,669
Of course, it wasn't just your beauty
that made me fall in love with you.

128
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:51,549
I fell even more in love with the beauty
and goodness of your heart, honey.

129
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:53,009
So, honey,

130
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:58,973
I want you to enjoy all of this,
every moment of this trip.

131
00:09:59,056 --> 00:10:00,933
Because all of this is for you.

132
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:03,644
For us, honey.

133
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:06,981
And I know you're not
a fan of long flights,

134
00:10:07,064 --> 00:10:10,943
and I know getting
your visa wasn't easy either.

135
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:11,902
It wasn't.

136
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:17,491
Thank you, honey.

137
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:31,422
That's what love can do, huh?

138
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:33,674
It makes you believe.

139
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:37,178
It makes you believe
in the beauty of the world.

140
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:40,514
Makes you believe even when
you haven't seen tomorrow yet.

141
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:54,153
Honey.

142
00:10:54,236 --> 00:10:58,240
Maybe we can just
take them somewhere safe?

143
00:10:58,324 --> 00:10:59,450
If that's okay with you.

144
00:11:01,285 --> 00:11:02,953
Sure, honey. It's up to you.

145
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:29,939
<i>I was just like that!</i>

146
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:33,859
<i>Love made me believe in it too!</i>

147
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,153
What a load of crap!

148
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,035
There's Alice.

149
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:47,123
She was taken by a syndicate.

150
00:11:50,209 --> 00:11:52,461
I used to hold on to hope, thinking

151
00:11:52,545 --> 00:11:55,047
there was something I could do,
that maybe I could still save her,

152
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:56,132
that maybe

153
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:58,717
we could still be together, that maybe

154
00:11:59,301 --> 00:12:01,262
I would still see her, but I didn't.

155
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:04,390
Because the world was never fair.

156
00:12:05,391 --> 00:12:08,018
The world was already unfair
before you were born.

157
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:11,105
Before any of this even came to be,
the world was already unfair!

158
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:13,357
Do you understand?

159
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:18,821
I understand.

160
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:23,659
So you.

161
00:12:24,326 --> 00:12:26,162
Don't you go getting weak on me.

162
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:29,373
Forget all those emotions.

163
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:30,583
It's all nonsense!

164
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:39,884
Whatever bond you have with everyone here,

165
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:41,719
whatever kindness they've shown you,

166
00:12:41,802 --> 00:12:44,722
whatever kindness Mikoy
and Chiara have shown you,

167
00:12:44,805 --> 00:12:46,098
forget all of it.

168
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:49,059
I don't even know.

169
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:53,314
They're crazy in love, thinking

170
00:12:53,397 --> 00:12:57,359
their illusion of love can change
the world, but it can't!

171
00:12:59,278 --> 00:13:00,112
What a load of crap.

172
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:02,948
It's all a load of crap.
Do you understand, Rahmboy?

173
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:07,953
So remember,

174
00:13:09,663 --> 00:13:11,582
what matters most of all

175
00:13:11,665 --> 00:13:14,835
is the plan we're all working on.

176
00:13:15,836 --> 00:13:17,505
Forget those emotions.

177
00:13:18,255 --> 00:13:19,590
They don't matter!

178
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:14,436
Oh?

179
00:14:17,314 --> 00:14:19,608
Carlota has a surprise.

180
00:14:19,692 --> 00:14:21,735
Looks like she's
coming back here to Albay.

181
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:34,373
because it's Chiara and Mikoy's wedding!

182
00:14:34,456 --> 00:14:36,500
- There you go, guys. Say hi!
- Hi!

183
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:39,128
Are you excited?

184
00:14:39,211 --> 00:14:40,170
- Of course.
- Chiara!

185
00:14:40,254 --> 00:14:43,841
Oh, my daughter looks beautiful!

186
00:14:43,924 --> 00:14:44,925
The bride!

187
00:14:45,009 --> 00:14:46,844
I don't want to be…

188
00:14:46,927 --> 00:14:48,929
Wait, we need to take a selfie.

189
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:50,472
- A groupie.
- Groupie, come on.

190
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:56,729
Oh!

191
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:59,356
Miss Minda should watch out.

192
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,400
I'm going to tease her
about how beautiful we look today.

193
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:03,611
See? I'll send this to her.

194
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:05,654
Is this good?

195
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:09,825
- One more?
- Sure.

196
00:15:16,373 --> 00:15:19,251
Today is Mikoy and Chiara's wedding.

197
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:23,047
And of course,
I'm here with the groom's team!

198
00:15:24,548 --> 00:15:25,382
Sir Mario, Angelito!

199
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:28,218
- Wave, guys! One more, say hi!
- Hello!

200
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:29,428
- Hello!
- Okay, picture, picture.

201
00:15:29,511 --> 00:15:31,639
There you go, looking sharp!

202
00:15:33,057 --> 00:15:34,600
Wave, kolokoys!

203
00:15:37,394 --> 00:15:39,521
Tess sent a groupie.

204
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,566
- Team bride.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa.

205
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:44,652
We can't let them beat us.
We need a team groom photo.

206
00:15:47,988 --> 00:15:49,239
- Get in position, get in position.
- Where's Mikoy?

207
00:15:49,323 --> 00:15:51,033
Mikoy?

208
00:15:51,116 --> 00:15:52,534
- Bro Mikoy.
- Mikoy!

209
00:16:13,013 --> 00:16:14,640
Looking handsome!

210
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:15,724
That's my bro!

211
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:25,859
You're shaking.

212
00:16:26,360 --> 00:16:27,444
Are you nervous?

213
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,822
A little, Dad.

214
00:16:30,864 --> 00:16:32,241
You can do this.

215
00:16:32,324 --> 00:16:33,701
Just be brave.

216
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:41,709
Love you too, son.

217
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,963
Okay, selfie time. Let's take a selfie.

218
00:16:46,046 --> 00:16:47,506
Groupie, groupie!

219
00:16:47,589 --> 00:16:49,550
- Groupie!
- Come here.

220
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:52,052
Come on.

221
00:16:54,263 --> 00:16:55,389
Wait, wait, wait.

222
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:57,057
- Rahmboy.
- Rahmboy.

223
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,435
That's right.

224
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:00,602
- That's right!
- Come, quick!

225
00:17:00,686 --> 00:17:01,687
You're family.

226
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:03,355
You're like one of the others.

227
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:05,858
Don't be an outsider. Come on!

228
00:17:05,941 --> 00:17:07,985
There!

229
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:15,617
Oh, your favorite!

230
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,460
Oh, wow!

231
00:17:24,543 --> 00:17:25,711
Chilimansi.

232
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:29,048
- Let's eat.
- Come on, let's eat.

233
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:31,175
Hey.

234
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:46,690
Posing for a photoshoot
is pretty tiring, huh?

235
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:48,692
I'm tired too!

236
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:49,777
Tell me about it.

237
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:52,404
My face was so tired
from smiling the whole time.

238
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:55,032
My facial muscles are exhausted.

239
00:17:56,575 --> 00:17:58,494
Good thing we can go for round three.

240
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:00,287
I didn't even make it to round four.

241
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:02,873
I plan to take home bacon. So good!

242
00:18:06,335 --> 00:18:08,504
I even had an egg cooked for me.

243
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:11,006
I told them to leave the yolk runny,

244
00:18:11,090 --> 00:18:14,009
but they still burned it. I ate it anyway.

245
00:18:14,093 --> 00:18:15,135
Still tasted good!

246
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:16,345
- Even if it's burnt.
- Yes.

247
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:17,846
You guys can't beat me.

248
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:18,931
Why?

249
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,478
You got takeout adobo?

250
00:18:24,978 --> 00:18:26,647
You're really something else.

251
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:28,482
How you did that?

252
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:30,609
Can’t be hungry.

253
00:18:31,735 --> 00:18:33,153
Sofie.

254
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:34,488
Yes, that’s Sofie.

255
00:18:36,782 --> 00:18:38,450
- It's Angelito.
- So…

256
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:39,576
Angelito.

257
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:42,162
Oh, right,

258
00:18:42,246 --> 00:18:44,039
my brother needs something.

259
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:46,208
I'll get back to you, okay?
I'll get back to you.

260
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:48,794
They're getting married?

261
00:18:48,877 --> 00:18:50,003
Why did he leave?

262
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:51,964
It's like they're avoiding each other.

263
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:53,757
Why are they avoiding each other?

264
00:18:53,841 --> 00:18:56,176
Didn't they just have a pretend wedding?

265
00:18:56,260 --> 00:18:57,886
A fake wedding that wasn't even real.

266
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:00,097
From a pretend wedding
to not talking to each other?

267
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:03,350
Just leave them be. That's how Gen Z is.

268
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:05,144
You know, when you're young

269
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:08,355
and you have a crush on your friend,

270
00:19:08,438 --> 00:19:11,275
you can't focus,
and of course, you're still shy.

271
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:12,818
Right?

272
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:14,528
All right.

273
00:19:25,747 --> 00:19:27,791
All we're missing is popcorn and beer.

274
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,876
But those are on the way too.

275
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:32,296
All we're missing are Agents Sianong,
Carlota, and Cocoy.

276
00:19:32,379 --> 00:19:33,922
Where are those guys?

277
00:19:34,006 --> 00:19:35,174
Good question.

278
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:44,141
Did you ask permission?

279
00:19:44,224 --> 00:19:46,935
No. As far as I know,
he doesn't come in on Saturdays.

280
00:20:01,575 --> 00:20:02,492
Brother Mikoy.

281
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:04,786
Hey.

282
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:10,459
You know, I'm going to miss you.

283
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:13,003
A lot.

284
00:20:16,215 --> 00:20:17,883
You're still my little boy.

285
00:20:18,550 --> 00:20:19,843
Look at me.

286
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:22,429
Come on, I'm not going anywhere.

287
00:20:22,512 --> 00:20:25,599
Your brother's just getting married, okay?

288
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:27,935
Wait.

289
00:20:29,353 --> 00:20:31,897
I know you won't forget about us.

290
00:20:33,982 --> 00:20:34,900
But I also know

291
00:20:37,027 --> 00:20:38,779
everything is going to change.

292
00:20:38,862 --> 00:20:39,947
Especially at home.

293
00:20:41,281 --> 00:20:43,951
Of course, it won't be the same as before.

294
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:49,748
But, Bro,

295
00:20:49,831 --> 00:20:50,749
you know…

296
00:20:54,836 --> 00:20:56,588
I'm so happy for you.

297
00:20:58,298 --> 00:20:59,424
Just think about it.

298
00:21:00,008 --> 00:21:01,218
Before,

299
00:21:03,011 --> 00:21:07,266
I used to wish that you would find a love

300
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:09,643
like Mom and Dad's.

301
00:21:12,688 --> 00:21:13,939
You're right.

302
00:21:14,022 --> 00:21:15,232
That's amazing!

303
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:17,985
You really manifested it, kid.

304
00:21:19,486 --> 00:21:20,821
I guess I did.

305
00:21:21,321 --> 00:21:22,572
So,

306
00:21:22,656 --> 00:21:24,616
I'm really, really happy for you.

307
00:21:25,742 --> 00:21:26,702
Because

308
00:21:27,995 --> 00:21:30,497
someone like you, who's so loving

309
00:21:31,081 --> 00:21:32,499
and such a good person,

310
00:21:32,582 --> 00:21:34,376
you truly deserve

311
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:41,675
Thank you, Angelito.

312
00:21:48,598 --> 00:21:51,059
Sorry, sir. We didn't get
to ask for your permission.

313
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:53,353
We promise we'll clean everything up.

314
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:02,529
Ray!

315
00:22:03,572 --> 00:22:04,906
Better yet,

316
00:22:05,407 --> 00:22:07,451
help me serve the food I brought

317
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:10,746
so our watch party
will be more fun, right?

318
00:22:10,829 --> 00:22:11,913
Come on!

319
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:25,177
A lot will change.

320
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:27,596
That's just part of life.

321
00:22:28,722 --> 00:22:29,681
And you,

322
00:22:29,765 --> 00:22:32,476
once you finish college,

323
00:22:32,559 --> 00:22:34,269
your world will open up even more!

324
00:22:34,352 --> 00:22:36,980
You'll have so many more opportunities.

325
00:22:37,064 --> 00:22:39,441
And you'll be able to explore, okay?

326
00:22:39,524 --> 00:22:41,485
Just promise me one thing.

327
00:22:41,568 --> 00:22:43,653
Whatever decision you make,

328
00:22:44,154 --> 00:22:45,989
whatever you do in life,

329
00:22:46,490 --> 00:22:50,160
just don't ever, ever, ever
give Mom and Dad a reason to worry.

330
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:54,414
And one more thing.

331
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:56,958
Whatever decision you make in life,

332
00:22:57,542 --> 00:22:59,044
no matter how difficult it may be,

333
00:22:59,544 --> 00:23:01,296
your decisions

334
00:23:01,379 --> 00:23:03,298
should always come from a place of love.

335
00:23:05,634 --> 00:23:06,468
Yes, bro.

336
00:23:10,555 --> 00:23:13,100
I've been proud of you
for a long time, Angelito.

337
00:23:13,934 --> 00:23:16,603
And I'm proud to have you as my brother.

338
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:28,365
Wait, you know what?

339
00:23:28,448 --> 00:23:30,951
I just remembered.
I have a gift for Chiara.

340
00:23:31,034 --> 00:23:31,952
Wait here, okay?

341
00:23:36,623 --> 00:23:38,291
- Bro.
- I'll leave this to you, okay?

342
00:23:38,375 --> 00:23:40,585
- I'll take care of it.
- Thanks.

343
00:24:12,075 --> 00:24:17,247
I went over your profiling report
on the immediate community in Albay.

344
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:20,834
It seems a little too ordinary.

345
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:24,921
Sometimes something ordinary can also mean

346
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:27,132
there's something too good to be true.

347
00:24:27,215 --> 00:24:28,842
Someone stood out to me.

348
00:24:28,925 --> 00:24:29,801
Who?

349
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:31,261
<i>That Rahmboy.</i>

350
00:24:38,935 --> 00:24:40,103
Sofie!

351
00:24:40,187 --> 00:24:41,605
The guy collapsed!

352
00:24:42,355 --> 00:24:43,607
Oh my! That guy!

353
00:24:45,442 --> 00:24:47,694
- <i>Senator, there's bad news.</i>
- What is it?

354
00:24:47,777 --> 00:24:49,863
<i>Viktor escaped, along with Donabel.</i>

355
00:24:49,946 --> 00:24:51,740
How did that happen? When?

356
00:24:51,823 --> 00:24:52,824
It was sudden.

357
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:55,452
Looks like someone up top
gave the go-ahead.

358
00:24:55,535 --> 00:24:58,246
And who are these annoying people?

359
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:03,251
Wait, guys, we have an update.

360
00:25:03,335 --> 00:25:05,253
Someone I know said

361
00:25:05,337 --> 00:25:08,006
someone broke
Viktor out last night. There.

362
00:25:10,217 --> 00:25:11,676
Looks like she escaped too.

363
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:13,929
What? What's happening?

364
00:25:14,429 --> 00:25:15,430
And who would break them out?

365
00:25:15,513 --> 00:25:17,557
Unless the Valtrovis are here.
